### VS Code ###
.vscode/
/uploads
# NOTE: /src/test was ignored here, which kept the entire test suite -- 24 files,
# 170 tests -- out of version control and alive only on one laptop. Same failure
# as the blanket *.sql rule below: a broad ignore silently excluding the files
# that matter most. Tests are tracked.
*.docx
*.md
# ...but the terms text is served to users and must be versioned with the code:
# it is the record of what each customer agreed to. Third time a blanket ignore
# has silently excluded something load-bearing, after *.sql and /src/test.
!src/main/resources/terms/*.md
*.db
# Keeps local dumps and scratch queries out of the repo...
*.sql
# ...but Flyway migrations are source, not data. Without this exception the
# blanket *.sql above silently excluded V5 onwards: they lived only on one
# laptop and never deployed, so their DROPs never ran anywhere (ddl-auto=update
# creates tables from entities, which masked the missing CREATEs but can never
# perform a drop).
!src/main/resources/db/migration/*.sql
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
src/main/resources/application-dev.properties
src/main/resources/application-dev.properties
*.properties
src/main/resources/application-dev.properties
src/main/resources/application-dev.properties
